  {"id":"ct-rosc-stemi","vignette":"After ROSC, the 12-lead ECG ten minutes later shows persistent ST elevation in the anterior leads. The patient remains comatose.","reasoning":"Persistent ST elevation with a suspected cardiac cause calls for emergency coronary angiography regardless of coma."}
